{"id":"9.3.2","doc":"T","title":"CPU Interrupts","words":484,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Each CPU has 32 interrupts, numbered from 0 ~ 31, including 26 peripheral interrupts and six internal interrupts."}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Peripheral interrupts: triggered by peripheral interrupt sources, include the following types:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Level-triggered interrupts: triggered by a high level signal."}]},{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The interrupt sources should hold the level till the CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" handles the interrupts."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Edge-triggered interrupts: triggered on a rising edge."}]},{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" responds to this kind of interrupts immediately."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"NMI interrupt: once triggered, the NMI interrupt can not be masked by software using the CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" internal registers."}]},{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"World Controller provides a way to mask this kind of interrupt."}]},{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For more information, see "},{"t":"xref","id":"16","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Chapter 16"}]},{"t":"text","v":" "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"World Controller (WCL)"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]}]]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Internal interrupts: generated inside CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":", include the following types:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Timer interrupts: triggered by internal timers and are used to generate periodic interrupts."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":12,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Software interrupts: triggered when software writes to special registers."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":13,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Profiling interrupt: triggered for performance monitoring and analysis."}]}]}]]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":14,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Level-triggered and edge-triggered both describe the ways of CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" to accept interrupt signals."}]},{"n":15,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For level-triggered interrupts, the level of interrupt signal should be kept till the CPU handles the interrupt, otherwise the interrupt may be lost."}]},{"n":16,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For edge-triggered interrupts, when a rising edge is detected, this edge will be recorded by CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":", which then allows the interrupt signal to be released."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":17,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Interrupt matrix routes the peripheral interrupt sources to any of the CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" peripheral interrupts."}]},{"n":18,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"By such way, CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" can receive the interrupt signals from peripheral interrupt sources."}]},{"n":19,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Table 9.3-2 lists all the interrupts and their types as well as priorities."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":20,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3 supports the above-mentioned 32 interrupts at six levels as shown in the table below."}]},{"n":21,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"A higher level corresponds to a higher priority."}]},{"n":22,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"NMI has the highest interrupt priority and once triggered, the CPU"},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"x"}]},{"t":"text","v":" must handle such interrupt."}],"warn":true},{"n":23,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Nested interrupts are also supported, i.e., low-level interrupts can be stopped by high-level interrupts."}]}]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 9.3-2. CPU Interrupts","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"No."}],[{"t":"text","v":"Category"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Type"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Priority"}